# Ontology Design Pattern: Sensor Observation
# ============================================
#
# Competency questions addressed by this pattern:
#   CQ1. Which sensor made a given observation?
#   CQ2. What feature of interest does an observation target?
#   CQ3. At what time was the result of an observation obtained?
#   CQ4. Which observations belong to the same observation collection?
#
# Classes intended: Sensor, Observation, FeatureOfInterest, Result,
#   ObservationCollection, Platform, Procedure, ObservableProperty.
# Object properties intended: madeBySensor, hasFeatureOfInterest,
#   hasResult, usedProcedure, hostedOn, memberOf.
# Datatype properties intended: resultTime, phenomenonTime, resultValue.
#
# Axiomatisation notes:
#   - Observation is disjoint from Sensor.
#   - Every Observation has exactly one result time.
#   - madeBySensor has domain Observation and range Sensor.
#
# Reuse: aligned with SOSA/SSN and DUL where possible.
# Licence: CC BY 4.0.  Author: anonymous.  Version: 1.0.0
#
